    "companies": "Google, Meta, Amazon, Microsoft, Apple",
    "desc": "Given a sequence, determine the optimal window satisfying the conditions for <strong>Longest Substring with At Least K Repeating Characters</strong>. Expand the right bound and contract the left bound dynamically.",
    "constraints": "• 1 <= s.length <= 10^5 or nums.length <= 10^5\n• Window values must satisfy constraint bounds.",
    "hints": "1. Maintain a frequency map or sum counter of the current window.\n2. Expand right pointer until the condition is met or violated.\n3. Contract left pointer to restore validity and record the best result.",
    "solution": "function longestSubstring(nums, k) {\n    if (!nums || nums.length === 0) return 0;\n    let left = 0, sum = 0, maxLen = 0;\n    const limit = (typeof k === 'number' ? k : 5);\n    for (let right = 0; right < nums.length; right++) {\n        sum += nums[right];\n        while (sum > limit && left <= right) {\n            sum -= nums[left++];\n        }\n        maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, right - left + 1);\n    }\n    return maxLen;\n}",
